    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters today\u2019s slate with a condensed starting core due to a heavy dose of difficult matchups and off-days. **Austin Riley** stands as our premier play at 64.25, capitalizing on a favorable matchup against Nick Martinez\u2019s 4.65 xERA. While his batting order slot at #7 marginally suppresses his upside, his ability to capitalize on platoon neutrality and park factors makes him the clear anchor for the lineup. **Isaac Paredes** (52.08) also earns a start in the UTIL spot; despite facing a high-caliber arm in Zack Wheeler, his projection is buoyed by a +9% dynamic platoon advantage and a premium spot in the #3 hole, which maximizes his opportunity to drive in runs even against elite competition. **Josh Naylor** (46.48) rounds out the trio, though he faces the toughest individual obstacle of the day in Jacob deGrom. While deGrom\u2019s 3.12 xERA necessitates caution, **Josh Naylor** remains in the lineup due to his high baseline and the lack of alternative high-floor production available.\n\nThe bench decision process today was largely defined by the optimizer\u2019s strict \"Zebras Floor\" threshold of 40.0. **Cole Young** was the most notable exclusion, coming in at a 32.80 score against deGrom. The combination of an elite opposing starter and a downward shift in his lineup positioning effectively neutralized the value of his sprint speed, keeping him out of the starting slots. We continue to monitor the status of **Corbin Carroll**, **James Wood**, and **Tyler Soderstrom**, who remain unavailable due to scheduling or injury, leaving our depth options like **Jose Caballero**, **Mickey Moniak**, and **Brice Turang** on the outside looking in as we preserve our daily game caps. With **Giancarlo Stanton**, **Seiya Suzuki**, **Trevor Story**, **Gabriel Moreno**, **Max Muncy**, **Dalton Rushing**, **Zach McKinstry**, **Griffin Conine**, **Edwin Arroyo**, and **Travis Bazzana** all seeing no action or limited projections, the strategy remains defensive; we are prioritizing high-efficiency matchups over volume to keep our WHIP and category averages protected in this late-season push. **Vinnie Pasquantino** is likewise held back today as we navigate the remaining game limits for the 2026 campaign.",
